WEBVTT

00:00:01.710 --> 00:00:02.671
Hi, I'm Dovetail!

00:00:02.671 --> 00:00:06.835
Today: a highlighter with no grammar that colours a whole file at once.

00:00:10.767 --> 00:00:14.829
Treat code as a one dimensional image, and label every part in parallel.

00:00:19.483 --> 00:00:23.525
A normal lexer walks one character at a time, with a grammar per language.

00:00:24.990 --> 00:00:29.225
gpu-lexer is never told the language, and labels every part at once.

00:00:31.175 --> 00:00:35.019
One CPU pass splits the source into words, spaces and symbols.

00:00:35.439 --> 00:00:38.631
On the GPU, each part becomes thirty two learned channels.

00:00:39.051 --> 00:00:41.762
A learned scan carries context in both directions.

00:00:42.251 --> 00:00:45.996
A tree merges blocks into one file summary, then sends it back down.

00:00:46.416 --> 00:00:50.522
Every part gets one of nine classes, and equal neighbours merge into spans.

00:00:51.775 --> 00:00:52.899
Here is the formula.

00:00:53.775 --> 00:00:56.109
The gate a decides how much old state survives.

00:00:56.822 --> 00:00:58.602
b is what the current part writes in.

00:00:59.674 --> 00:01:02.609
Two of these maps in a row are still one map, so

00:01:02.609 --> 00:01:05.054
any stretch of code shrinks to two numbers per channel.

00:01:06.775 --> 00:01:08.697
Cut the parts into blocks of thirty two.

00:01:09.484 --> 00:01:11.999
Fold every block into one pair, all at once.

00:01:12.637 --> 00:01:14.831
A short scan tells each block where it starts.

00:01:15.251 --> 00:01:17.018
Each block replays from its true start.

00:01:19.050 --> 00:01:21.141
Here is the tree from Shu Ding's animation.

00:01:21.561 --> 00:01:24.206
Whole file context comes back down to every part.

00:01:25.717 --> 00:01:29.906
On five and a half million characters, gpu-lexer takes about two

00:01:29.906 --> 00:01:31.429
hundred and twenty milliseconds.

00:01:31.429 --> 00:01:33.333
Highlights takes about seventy five.

00:01:34.383 --> 00:01:36.080
And the three point eight times?

00:01:36.080 --> 00:01:39.192
Measured the same way before and after, the code is worth

00:01:39.192 --> 00:01:40.323
one point three seven.

00:01:41.933 --> 00:01:45.855
These maps compose into maps of the same size, so the scan never grows.

00:01:50.650 --> 00:01:52.811
Code as an image, one scan, one tree.

00:01:55.250 --> 00:01:57.429
Every source is in the full article.

00:01:57.429 --> 00:01:58.052
I'm Dovetail.

00:01:58.052 --> 00:01:58.363
Bye!
